<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia May 1-20 palm oil exports 383,956t - SGS.</title>
<headline>Malaysia May 1-20 palm oil exports 383,956t - SGS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo surveyor Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS) Malaysia Sdn Bhd said it estimated Malaysia's palm oil exports for May 1-20 at 383,956 tonnes against 429,661 tonnes for April 1-20.</p>
<p>It said the exports comprised 102,956 tonnes of RBD palm oil, 173,454 tonnes of RBD palm olein and 30,779 tonnes of RBD palm stearin. The other products totalled 76,767 tonnes.  </p>
<p>India was the top buyer during the period, taking 85,070 tonnes, followed by Pakistan which bought 62,750 tonnes, China (43,100 tonnes) and Japan (35,250 tonnes).</p>
<p>Countries in the European Union bought 35,594 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-7510)</p>
</text>
